  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14208490/assets/9dbee02f0c07041dd8424faf683952ada2f7f1a604f9bf89a65588eaf3b6f9f6.png)\n\nThe legs of an isosceles right triangle are increasing. The length, measured in feet, of each leg is given by $x(t)=t+{t}^{2},$ where $t>0$ is the time in seconds. What is the rate of the change of the length of the hypotenuse after $2$ seconds? Give your answer rounded to $1$ decimal place.",
